      "math_academy_id": "q-72689",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Noah removes some food from his freezer to defrost. The temperature of the food was $-{4.6}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ After a few hours, the temperature of the food increased by ${10.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ What was the temperature of the food after those few hours?",
      "worked_solution": "To determine the temperature of the food after a few hours, we add the variation in temperature to the initial temperature of the food. This gives\n\n$$\n-{4.6}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}+{10.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}={5.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the temperature of the food after a few hours was ${5.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$",
